1
00:00:01,068 --> 00:00:02,991
Taming a Tank

2
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:08,679
Hey, Buster Gallon. When did you get to Crest's laboratory? Did you quit farming already?

3
00:00:08,679 --> 00:00:11,967
Absolutely not. Why would I quit when my watermelons are selling like hotcakes?

4
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,128
Yeah, they were delicious.

5
00:00:13,227 --> 00:00:18,533
The Beast Virus that makes Metal Cardbots go berserk... and the vaccine that will conquer that virus.

6
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:22,890
As a genius scientist and inventor, how could I possibly just sit back and do nothing after hearing the news?

7
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:25,202
Thanks to him, we're greatly accelerating the development of the vaccine.

8
00:00:25,202 --> 00:00:26,565
See?

9
00:00:26,565 --> 00:00:28,507
- That sounds good and all, but...
- Hi, Mini Gallons!

10
00:00:28,507 --> 00:00:32,923
Ah, and it'd be helpful if Deep Bite could come here, too. How about tomorrow?

11
00:00:32,923 --> 00:00:37,478
Uh, sure! That'll be fine. By the way, there's something I need to tell you.

12
00:00:37,478 --> 00:00:38,850
Hm? What's that?

13
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:40,466
You see...

14
00:00:40,466 --> 00:00:41,753
W-what?!

15
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:44,042
My sister transferred to your school?!

16
00:00:44,042 --> 00:00:45,246
We're the ones who were surprised the most, you know.

17
00:00:45,246 --> 00:00:48,679
We had no idea that Soleil was your younger twin sister...

18
00:00:48,679 --> 00:00:50,405
Who on Earth told you that?

19
00:00:50,405 --> 00:00:52,871
Your mom told us, of course!

20
00:00:52,871 --> 00:00:53,646
My mother?!

21
00:00:53,646 --> 00:00:58,667
Dr. Rhea Cayenne! The leading authority on robotics! I even got her autograph!

22
00:00:59,365 --> 00:01:00,612
(So that's how it happened...)

23
00:01:00,612 --> 00:01:04,736
It'll still take some time to develop a vaccine. Until then, take care of my sister.

24
00:01:04,736 --> 00:01:06,278
Uh, wait!

25
00:01:06,278 --> 00:01:08,390
- That didn't go as expected.
- Man...

26
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:11,692
I was hoping Soleil's brother would have stepped in to resolve the situation...

27
00:01:11,692 --> 00:01:13,111
GRRRRAAHH!!

28
00:01:13,111 --> 00:01:14,310
What was that?!

29
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:17,563
Grrr!! GRRR!!

30
00:01:17,563 --> 00:01:20,114
I'm gonna crush every single bozo I set my eyes on!!

31
00:01:20,114 --> 00:01:24,051
Stop! This is how you repay me after I fixed and fed you?!

32
00:01:24,051 --> 00:01:25,718
Such a savage.

33
00:01:25,718 --> 00:01:28,859
He hasn’t lost one bit of his wild instincts even after being sealed, I'll give him that.

34
00:01:28,859 --> 00:01:31,093
This isn't the time to be impressed...

35
00:01:31,093 --> 00:01:33,252
Jun! I'll go try to calm Tigun down.

36
00:01:33,252 --> 00:01:34,896
Okay. I'm counting on you.

37
00:01:36,444 --> 00:01:39,554
Stop this, Tigun! There's no need to fight anymore!

38
00:01:39,554 --> 00:01:43,021
Shaddap! Grrrrr!!

39
00:01:45,854 --> 00:01:50,311
I'm-a tiger! A wild tiger listens to nobody!

40
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:56,262
Blue Cop!

41
00:01:56,561 --> 00:01:59,756
Jun, can't you just keep him in your Metal Breath?

42
00:01:59,756 --> 00:02:01,700
Eheheh... just give me a moment.

43
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,977
Jun! Time for a player substitution!

44
00:02:02,977 --> 00:02:04,441
Uh, I'll go too!

45
00:02:04,441 --> 00:02:06,444
Shut up already!

46
00:02:06,444 --> 00:02:06,930
Uh-

47
00:02:07,031 --> 00:02:07,992
AUGH!

48
00:02:07,992 --> 00:02:11,580
Grrrrrhahaha!! I'm a free tiger now!

49
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,657
Grrrrr!!

50
00:02:12,657 --> 00:02:15,098
- Grrrrhahahaha!!
- Where are you going?!

51
00:02:16,098 --> 00:02:16,806
Huh?!

52
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:22,401
It's a cat!

53
00:02:22,401 --> 00:02:27,687
Wh-what the heck are you, now? Ya think a little runt like you can take on ME? Tigun?!

54
00:02:27,687 --> 00:02:30,401
Oh, we're doin' this? I'll crush you beneath my feet!

55
00:02:30,401 --> 00:02:31,483
No, Tigun!!

56
00:02:33,691 --> 00:02:37,519
I won't forgive anyone who tries to take a life so carelessly!

57
00:02:37,519 --> 00:02:38,699
Dexter!

58
00:02:40,864 --> 00:02:42,316
It's okay now.

59
00:02:48,062 --> 00:02:50,175
That was a close one, wasn't it?

60
00:02:50,175 --> 00:02:52,985
What gives, Dexter? What brings you to the car center today?

61
00:02:52,985 --> 00:02:58,081
I was working on a building demolition nearby, and I kept hearing the sound of cannon fire coming from the area.

62
00:02:58,081 --> 00:03:02,531
It sounded like it was coming from the direction of Edo's car center, so I rushed over. And what do you know, it was total chaos.

63
00:03:02,631 --> 00:03:04,461
That jerk!

64
00:03:05,632 --> 00:03:07,747
That was one smooth bonk to the head.

65
00:03:07,747 --> 00:03:09,080
You just came here for the cats, didn't you?

66
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:12,925
The neighborhood cats often gather at uncle Edo's car center, don't they?

67
00:03:12,925 --> 00:03:15,393
Ahem. I suppose that's not untrue...

68
00:03:15,393 --> 00:03:18,460
Either way, it's all thanks to you that it was resolved safely without incident.

69
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:21,245
What do you mean, "without incident"?! What am I gonna do with that huge mess out there?!

70
00:03:21,245 --> 00:03:23,228
That guy caused me a massive loss!

71
00:03:23,228 --> 00:03:25,346
I'm-a wild tigerrrr....

72
00:03:25,346 --> 00:03:28,616
That's a Wild Cardbot, isn't it? You sealed him?

73
00:03:28,616 --> 00:03:30,937
Yeah. But he still went on a rampage anyway.

74
00:03:30,937 --> 00:03:36,060
You let him go on a rampage like that again, and I'm gonna tell the mayor that we can't get along with the likes of him!

75
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,353
No, you can't!

76
00:03:37,353 --> 00:03:43,513
Wild Cardbot or Metal Cardbot, it doesn't matter anymore. I will banish everyone from the planet Machina! (FX-italic)

77
00:03:43,513 --> 00:03:44,646
B-banish?!

78
00:03:44,646 --> 00:03:46,663
Bye bye~! (FX-italic)

79
00:03:47,263 --> 00:03:50,031
No!! I don't want to break through the atmosphere ever again!

80
00:03:50,031 --> 00:03:51,509
Calm down, Phoenix Fire!

81
00:03:51,509 --> 00:03:52,798
- You hear me?!
- Kitty chose me!

82
00:03:52,798 --> 00:03:55,026
- Sigh... yeah, yeah.
- Kitty chose me!

83
00:03:56,026 --> 00:03:58,194
Tigun, come on back.

84
00:03:58,194 --> 00:04:01,048
I'll take him with me. You happy now?

85
00:04:01,048 --> 00:04:04,473
Good grief. You should've done that from the start. Just get him out of here.

86
00:04:04,473 --> 00:04:07,852
I'll leave the checkups on Phoenix Fire and Deep Bite to you, then.

87
00:04:07,852 --> 00:04:10,151
Uh... I'd like you to take a look at my temperature sensor.

88
00:04:10,151 --> 00:04:11,936
I want a full dental scaling, please.

89
00:04:11,936 --> 00:04:15,127
Fine, fine. At least it's better than babysitting a tiger.

90
00:04:15,127 --> 00:04:16,588
Oh! Me first!

91
00:04:16,990 --> 00:04:20,588
Let's go, Blue Cop. Anna, Theo, we're going now!

92
00:04:20,588 --> 00:04:21,415
Jun!

93
00:04:21,841 --> 00:04:24,394
Jun really puts up with a lot, huh.

94
00:04:24,394 --> 00:04:25,360
Yeah...

95
00:04:27,677 --> 00:04:29,403
Anna! Good morning!

96
00:04:29,403 --> 00:04:32,233
Good morning! Uh... Jun?

97
00:04:33,627 --> 00:04:34,927
A-are you okay?

98
00:04:34,927 --> 00:04:35,648
Ugh...

99
00:04:35,648 --> 00:04:37,387
He said he couldn't sleep at all last night.

100
00:04:37,387 --> 00:04:38,800
Really?

101
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:43,136
Tigun kept on shouting inside the Metal Breath all night long...

102
00:04:43,136 --> 00:04:45,374
Oi! Someone there?! Answer me, now!!

103
00:04:45,374 --> 00:04:46,148
- Be quiet...
- Grrrah!!

104
00:04:46,148 --> 00:04:48,963
- Be quiet...
- This thing's so cramped, I can't breathe! Get me outta here right now!!!

105
00:04:48,963 --> 00:04:51,358
Do you even realize how late it is?! Shut it!!

106
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:52,781
It's suffocating in here!!

107
00:04:52,781 --> 00:04:53,914
Get me outta here! 

108
00:04:53,914 --> 00:04:54,614
Get me outta here! Let me out!

109
00:04:54,614 --> 00:04:55,773
Get me outta here! Let me out! Letmeoutletmeoutletmeouttahere!!

110
00:04:55,773 --> 00:04:56,931
Get me outta here! Let me out! Letmeoutletmeoutletmeouttahere!! Isaidgetmeouttahere!

111
00:04:56,931 --> 00:04:58,090
Get me outta here! Let me out! Letmeoutletmeoutletmeouttahere!! Isaidgetmeouttahere! Nownownow!!

112
00:04:58,090 --> 00:04:59,249
Get me outta here! Let me out! Letmeoutletmeoutletmeouttahere!! Isaidgetmeouttahere! Nownownow!! Grrrrrrrrr!!!

113
00:05:04,105 --> 00:05:06,923
- Yawn... what's all the racket?
- Get me out!! Grrrrrr!!

114
00:05:07,023 --> 00:05:08,831
Our fridge might be malfunctioning...

115
00:05:08,831 --> 00:05:09,612
Let's have a look...

116
00:05:09,612 --> 00:05:10,228
GRRRAH!!!

117
00:05:10,228 --> 00:05:11,000
AAAHHHH!!

118
00:05:12,110 --> 00:05:15,449
Jun! You can't be putting tigers in the fridge!

119
00:05:15,449 --> 00:05:18,845
This is going to bother the neighbors. Try to fix this somehow...

120
00:05:18,845 --> 00:05:20,223
Okay...

121
00:05:20,223 --> 00:05:21,896
Jun. Jun!

122
00:05:21,896 --> 00:05:22,822
What?

123
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:23,949
I have an idea.

124
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:24,810
Eh?

125
00:05:25,011 --> 00:05:27,168
So you took him for a drive all night?

126
00:05:27,168 --> 00:05:31,651
That idiot, Tigun... He kept throwing a tantrum even while we were driving.

127
00:05:31,651 --> 00:05:34,877
That's why I didn't sleep at all last night...

128
00:05:34,877 --> 00:05:36,307
You’re such a fool.

129
00:05:36,307 --> 00:05:41,038
If he won’t listen, just force him to follow your command. Your Metal Breath must have that function, right?

130
00:05:41,038 --> 00:05:43,268
I know. I just don't want to use it.

131
00:05:43,268 --> 00:05:47,273
My mother once said that machines only have value when you use them to their full potential.

132
00:05:47,273 --> 00:05:49,441
They’re not machines! They’re friends!

133
00:05:49,441 --> 00:05:50,052
Friends...?

134
00:05:50,052 --> 00:05:53,403
Yeah! F-R-I-E-N-D-S! They have hearts and feelings, too.

135
00:05:53,403 --> 00:05:57,401
Even if they were born on different planets or come in different sizes, if your hearts connect, you can become friends!

136
00:05:57,401 --> 00:06:03,946
I don’t understand. He doesn’t listen to a word you say, and he doesn't provide you with anything of value. How can you call him a “friend”?

137
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:06,978
Do you even understand what a friend is?

138
00:06:06,978 --> 00:06:10,269
You calmed down Blue Cop when he went berserk, and you gave him back to me!

139
00:06:11,470 --> 00:06:13,658
...your dearest friend. Right? (FX-italic)

140
00:06:13,658 --> 00:06:17,298
Why did you do that? I thought you understood those feelings between me and Blue Cop!

141
00:06:17,298 --> 00:06:18,141
That was...

142
00:06:18,141 --> 00:06:19,932
Aren't you and Blaion friends?

143
00:06:19,932 --> 00:06:20,612
What?

144
00:06:20,612 --> 00:06:22,567
That is none of your business.

145
00:06:22,567 --> 00:06:25,379
Yes. Yes it is, Blaion. Why do you follow Soleil's-

146
00:06:25,379 --> 00:06:28,250
SHADDAP!!! Just get me outta here!!

147
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:29,276
Grrrrr!! Grrrrrrrrraahhh!!!

148
00:06:29,276 --> 00:06:35,067
- Dang it, not again! I'll just go back home. Please tell our teacher what happened, guys.
- Get me out!! Lemme out!!

149
00:06:35,067 --> 00:06:36,223
- Ahaha... alright.
- Lemme ouuuuut!!

150
00:06:36,223 --> 00:06:37,648
- Be careful on your way home!
- Grraaaaghhh!!

151
00:06:38,048 --> 00:06:40,646
Blue Cop is my dearest friend! (FX-italic)

152
00:06:40,646 --> 00:06:42,494
Jun is also my dearest friend. (FX-italic)

153
00:06:42,494 --> 00:06:44,382
Looks like you two are really close! (FX-italic)

154
00:06:49,598 --> 00:06:54,519
This car was kept for spare parts... but now look at it. It's not even good enough to be used for scrap now!

155
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:55,819
How about we get another one for you?

156
00:06:55,819 --> 00:06:58,754
There's a bunch of cars rolling around this town. I'll go grab one for you.

157
00:06:58,754 --> 00:07:00,432
Hey! You can't do that!

158
00:07:00,432 --> 00:07:02,701
I was just messing with you. Hahaha!

159
00:07:02,701 --> 00:07:04,886
I'm back, Edo.

160
00:07:04,886 --> 00:07:06,971
I figured you ran out of these by now. Here you go.

161
00:07:06,971 --> 00:07:09,088
Ugh. Bring it this way.

162
00:07:09,466 --> 00:07:12,314
Thanks for taking care of these homeless kitties, Edo.

163
00:07:12,314 --> 00:07:17,711
Well, I can't exactly kick them out. Until someone comes along to adopt them, they'll be just like family to me.

164
00:07:17,711 --> 00:07:19,406
They're just like you guys in that way, right?

165
00:07:19,406 --> 00:07:20,391
Edo.

166
00:07:20,391 --> 00:07:24,478
Thanks to Jun, I started to think that I can trust humans on this planet.

167
00:07:24,478 --> 00:07:25,848
So please don't push him too hard-

168
00:07:25,848 --> 00:07:29,557
Don't be silly! I took care of him ever since he was as small as a peanut.

169
00:07:29,557 --> 00:07:32,788
I know better than anyone about what he can handle.

170
00:07:32,788 --> 00:07:35,220
He's like family to me too, after all!

171
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,778
By the way, I don't see Nightcrawler...

172
00:07:36,778 --> 00:07:39,516
Night... what? Were you listening to me?

173
00:07:39,516 --> 00:07:42,220
I don't see the black one. You know, the one who tried to fight Tigun.

174
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:45,494
Don't worry about her. Look. There she is.

175
00:07:45,494 --> 00:07:48,009
Nightcrawler! So that's where you were!

176
00:07:48,965 --> 00:07:50,110
Huh?

177
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:55,057
Edo, look! I can see why she tried to fight Tigun. Call Jun right away!

178
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:56,937
Huh? Uh, oh, right.

179
00:07:57,137 --> 00:07:57,867
- What do you want to do today?
- Let's see...

180
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:58,442
- What do you want to do today?
- Let's see...

181
00:07:58,442 --> 00:07:59,362
ROAR!!!

182
00:07:59,463 --> 00:08:00,336
Huh?

183
00:08:00,336 --> 00:08:01,031
Was that a tiger?

184
00:08:01,031 --> 00:08:04,798
GRRRRAAARRRR!

185
00:08:04,898 --> 00:08:07,108
- Hey, uncle Edo...
- GRRR! GRRRR!!

186
00:08:07,108 --> 00:08:08,610
- What's up?
- GRRRRRRRRR!!

187
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:09,968
- Yeah. Yeah...
- GRAAHHHH!! Lemme out lemme out!!

188
00:08:09,968 --> 00:08:11,836
- Are you sure?
- GRAAHHHH!! Lemme out lemme out!!

189
00:08:11,836 --> 00:08:14,290
- Okay. I'll see you later.
- GRRARRRARRRGHH!!

190
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:16,403
- Ugh... Alright, Tigun.
- GRAHHH!! Lemme outta here already!! Out!!

191
00:08:16,403 --> 00:08:19,314
- I'll let you out, okay? Just give me a minute.
- GRAHHH!! Lemme outta here already!! Out!!

192
00:08:19,314 --> 00:08:20,112
Wait, really?

193
00:08:20,112 --> 00:08:20,846
Ugh.

194
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,257
Tigun. Come out.

195
00:08:32,110 --> 00:08:35,620
GRAH! Fresh air really is the best!

196
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:38,153
It's time to go wild aga- eh?

197
00:08:38,153 --> 00:08:40,921
What are you all doing? You guys look like ya wanna fight me or something.

198
00:08:40,921 --> 00:08:42,586
Sounds good to me- What the?

199
00:08:42,586 --> 00:08:45,764
You! Giraffe! You're the one who pulled off a surprise attack on me, aren't ya?!

200
00:08:45,764 --> 00:08:48,216
It was necessary to protect many lives.

201
00:08:48,216 --> 00:08:53,687
Who cares! Sure, I can't use my wild powers at will anymore, but don’t you dare underestimate me! Grrrr-

202
00:08:53,687 --> 00:08:55,584
Hold it. Look here.

203
00:08:56,687 --> 00:08:59,663
Grr? You're the tiny punk who had the nerve to pick a fight with me!

204
00:08:59,663 --> 00:09:03,894
Gah! It's multiplying! Is it using the same technique as Phantom Hornet?!

205
00:09:03,894 --> 00:09:04,705
No...

206
00:09:04,705 --> 00:09:05,615
- Meow!
- Gr-?!

207
00:09:05,615 --> 00:09:11,745
Nightcrawler is a mother. She picked a fight with you because she wanted to protect her children. Do you get it now?

208
00:09:11,745 --> 00:09:13,533
Mo... mother? So what!

209
00:09:13,533 --> 00:09:14,120
Meow!

210
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:14,897
Gaaahh!

211
00:09:14,897 --> 00:09:16,956
What, you scared of her?

212
00:09:16,956 --> 00:09:17,913
They're so cute, though!

213
00:09:17,913 --> 00:09:22,493
Mothers and fathers alike will do anything to protect their children.

214
00:09:22,493 --> 00:09:24,423
Get away from me! Don't come near!

215
00:09:24,423 --> 00:09:25,758
Those... those eyes...

216
00:09:25,758 --> 00:09:29,591
They look like two suns burning bright through the darkness!

217
00:09:29,591 --> 00:09:34,706
Her eyes reveal a strength of will that’s far greater than mine or any other Wild Cardbot, who only fight for the sake of fighting!

218
00:09:34,706 --> 00:09:37,533
Is this what they call... the resolve of the protector?!

219
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:38,513
Meow!

220
00:09:38,513 --> 00:09:40,480
Gaaah!! It's too powerful!! Grrrraaahhh!!

221
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:43,389
Looks like even Wild Cardbots can't beat the power of love.

222
00:09:43,389 --> 00:09:45,605
Tigun. Let's live together on this planet.

223
00:09:45,605 --> 00:09:50,134
Yeah! We should be friends and work together towards a new future!

224
00:09:50,134 --> 00:09:54,859
Friends? I'm just a lone beast that fights until he dies!

225
00:09:54,859 --> 00:09:56,287
Be a lone beast, then.

226
00:09:56,287 --> 00:09:59,913
We'll be your mom and dad, and we'll protect and take care of you until the end.

227
00:09:59,913 --> 00:10:01,014
Tigun.

228
00:10:01,014 --> 00:10:02,115
You can call me mom.

229
00:10:02,115 --> 00:10:03,389
Don't be weird, Blue Cop.

230
00:10:03,389 --> 00:10:04,537
And uncle Edo is your dad!

231
00:10:04,537 --> 00:10:04,971
Eh?!

232
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:08,345
P-protect me? Bwahahahaha!

233
00:10:08,345 --> 00:10:15,317
I am a Wild Cardbot! You'll never know when I might bare my claws against you Metal Cardbots, my eternal foes!

234
00:10:15,317 --> 00:10:18,926
If you do that, I'll just blame my poor judgement and give up on you!

235
00:10:18,926 --> 00:10:19,398
Wh-?!

236
00:10:19,398 --> 00:10:22,418
- Oh...
- Jun! That isn't something to joke about!

237
00:10:22,418 --> 00:10:26,643
I believe in you, Tigun. So please, believe in me too!

238
00:10:26,974 --> 00:10:31,105
Grrrr... Protect me, huh...?

239
00:10:34,172 --> 00:10:37,407
Guess it can't hurt to try living a life where fighting isn't everything.

240
00:10:40,028 --> 00:10:41,211
Thank you, Tigun- Oh!

241
00:10:41,211 --> 00:10:42,855
Meow! Meow!

242
00:10:43,355 --> 00:10:45,298
W-wait, wait- Ow!!

243
00:10:45,298 --> 00:10:48,048
First he'll need to learn how to get along with Nightcrawler.

244
00:10:48,048 --> 00:10:50,091
Hahahaha!

245
00:10:50,091 --> 00:10:53,725
Hm. I came here because I smelled a fight brewing with Mr. Tigun,

246
00:10:53,725 --> 00:10:56,740
but what in the world am I looking at? Being all warmhearted and friendly...

247
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,321
What a disappointment!

248
00:10:59,758 --> 00:11:03,551
Not like that! Act like you're on a real hunt! Chomp it! Pounce on it and chomp it!

249
00:11:03,551 --> 00:11:06,344
That's right! Use your claws too! Pull out your full arsenal!

250
00:11:06,344 --> 00:11:08,759
What in the world happened here?

251
00:11:08,759 --> 00:11:12,100
The same Tigun that only knew how to rampage, is now playing with kittens.

252
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:14,197
He looks like a dad playing with his babies.

253
00:11:14,197 --> 00:11:15,940
He's better than my dad!

254
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:20,014
Alright, kids! The great Tigun will teach ya what a real hunt looks like!

255
00:11:20,014 --> 00:11:20,893
ROAR!!

256
00:11:20,893 --> 00:11:22,177
Meow!

257
00:11:22,177 --> 00:11:22,988
GRRRRRRRRR!!

258
00:11:22,988 --> 00:11:23,831
Meowmeowmeowmeow!

259
00:11:23,831 --> 00:11:26,461
Hey, hey, just don't break anything around here, alright?

260
00:11:26,461 --> 00:11:27,955
Okay, Papa Edo!

261
00:11:27,955 --> 00:11:29,225
I said call me big bro Edo! Big bro!!

262
00:11:29,225 --> 00:11:31,144
Follow me! Time for the next lesson!

263
00:11:31,144 --> 00:11:31,865
ROARRRR!!

264
00:11:31,865 --> 00:11:34,038
Meow!
